      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-03-16_WidnesExaminer_art0037" n="art0037">
        <head>District League.</head>
        <p>District League.</p>
        <p>LANCASHIRE COMBINATION.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON "A" V BROUGHTON BANGERS "A." —This match was spoiled by a heavy downpour of rain ou Saturday, but there was a crowd of quite 2,000 on the Warrington ground. Warrington started in promising style, Jolley showing up well at centre. The halves shaped poorly behind the pack however, and the attack had no sting. Critchley and Jolley both failed at penalty shots for goal, and half-time arrived with the score sheet blank. The around was in a sorry state on resuming, and the home pl. Ayers seemed to be unable to vary their play at all. Broughton shaped much better, Beetham leading the forwards well, and eventually Keefe dribbled over, for Howarth to kick a goal. But for Brown's plucky defence at full-back, the score would have been larger. Final : Broughton A" 5 paints, Warringtsn " A" nil.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-03-16_WidnesExaminer_art0038" n="art0038">
        <head>LANCASHIRE SHIELD.</head>
        <p>LANCASHIRE SHIELD.</p>
        <p>Roches,le H 0 3 9 Pemberton ...... 0 0 0 Runcorn "A" 2 2 10 Wigan llighfield 0 0 0 RIINCoRN " A" v WIGAN HIGHFIFLD.—Runcorn put almost a senior team in the field at Ilighfield against the Wigan Juniors, but were only able to MOTO an equalising try in the second half.—The replay at Runcarn on Monday attracted 1.000 spectators, and Highfield again played a plucky game. but were compelled to admit Runcorn's superiority. Massey scored a try and Moran a goal for the homsters in the first half ; Inman scored a second try, and Moran again goaled. Atherton and Smith were prominent for the visitors, but failed to score. Enal : Runcorn, 10 points; Wigan Hightleld, nil. RYLANDS' TEAM TO-DAY.</p>
        <p>RYLAND Ir. BARTON.-At Gorsey-lane. Brarnhall ; Griffiths, Leah, Horrocks, Hennessey ; Gallop, Floyd ; Bramwcod, Bootb,Stretford,Morris, Mason, Broadhurst.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-03-16_WidnesExaminer_art0039" n="art0039">
        <head>ASSOCIATION FOOTBALL.</head>
        <p>ASSOCIATION FOOTBALL.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON MEDAL COMPETITION. FIRST ROUND.</p>
        <p>ORTORD WRITE STAR V. IBANK QUAY RECREATION. This match at Orford on Saturday ended in a victory for the home team by three goals to one, the scorers being Jackson (2) and Williams for the wieners, and Eastwood for the losers.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-03-16_WidnesExaminer_art0040" n="art0040">
        <head>ALTRINCHAM DISTRICT LEAGUE. FIRST DIVISION. RESULTS TO DATE.</head>
        <p>ALTRINCHAM DISTRICT LEAGUE. FIRST DIVISION. RESULTS TO DATE.</p>
        <p>Goal.</p>
        <p>P. W. L. D. F. A. PTS. Mobberlev 2O .14 . 4 9.. 54 ... 31 ...30 Bowdon Vale 18 .13 . 3 2.. 46 ... 31 .. 28 Latchford l9 ...12 ... 5 ... 2 ... 47 ... 26 ...26 Lymm l7 .11 3 3.. 43 28 —25 Lostock Gralam —l5 —ll ... 2 ... 2 ... 83 ... 18 ...24 Broadheath 17 . 8 .. 6 ... 3 ... 44 ... 31 ...19 Oughtrington Am' 19 ... 6 ...10 ... 3 ... 30 ... 32 ...15 Ougbtrington Parkls ... 6 ... 7 ... 2 ... 31 ... 25 —ll St. Vincent's lB .. 4 8 ... 6 ... 19 ... 31 ...14 Altrincham Lads l6 ... 5 —ll. ... 0 ... 21 ... 44 ...10 Sale Albion 18 . 3 ...12 ... 3 ... 28 ... 47 ... 9 Penketh l5 ... 2 ...12 ... 1 ... 13 ... 52 ... 5 Kuutsford St orossls ... 0 ...12 ... 3 ... 21 ... 97 ... 3</p>
        <p>BROADDRATII V. BOWDON VALE. At Navigation-road, Altrincharn, on Saturday. Result : Bowdon Vale, two ; Broadheatb, one.</p>
        <p>ALTRIECTIAM LADS V. MOBBERLEY. On Stamford Park, Altrincbam.—The final being Afobberley, four; Altrincbam Lads, one. ALTRINCHAM JUNIOR COMPETITION. LATOHFORD V. ALTRINCHAM AMATEURS.</p>
        <p>_ This re-played tie took place at Latchford before a fair crowd. Like the previous meeting, vthich ended in goalless draw, tbis one was of a close and even nature all through, there being little to choose between the contestants. In the end the home team—Latcliford— gained the verdict by a goal to nil ; thus qualifying to meet Lymm Lads on Saturday next in the semi-flual tie.</p>
