      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-03-16_WidnesExaminer_art0041" n="art0041">
        <head>RIFLE SHOOTING.</head>
        <p>RIFLE SHOOTING.</p>
        <p>APPLETON RIFLE CLUR.—N.R.A. COMPETITION. The fifth, and final, of rk series of monthly Competi- tions, organized by the National Rifle Assooiation, took place on the Wbitecross Range, the other evening, (Friday, March Bth), by termission of the officials. Mr A E Perry, one of the officials, acted as umpire. The conditions of the Competition were :—A team of six men ; ten shots at a decimal target, at 25 yards possible score per man, 100 ;the centre of the shot-hole to determine the value of the shot; no sighting shot allowed. Below are the individual and total scores S James S Pollard 93 J W Plinston A Shepherd 9O F C Bennion C P Day 545</p>
