        <p>WARRINGTON BLUE COAT CHARITY SCHOOL. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the TRUSTEES of the above SCHOOL will, at their next Quarterly Meeting, on the 15th day of April next, proceed to elect Eight Children (3 Boys and 5 Girls) to Vacancies now existing in the Institution. No Candidate will be eligible unless an application on his or her behalf (forms of which may he obtained from the Clerk, at his Office, 3, Winwick Street), shall have been made to the Clerk to the Trustees, at least fourteen days previous to the day of Meeting. In electing Children, the Trustees make Orphans their first choice. Those deprived of one parent come next in consideration, and after them the children of parents who have the greatest number and the slenderest 'means. Dated this 15th day of March, 1912. HENRY GREENALL, Clerk to the Trustees.</p>
