        <p>ODDFELLOWS CELEBRATION. A supper and social was held by the members of the "Loyal Trafford "Lodge of the Independent Order of Oddfellows (Manchester Unity), at the Bridgewater Arms on Saturday evening to celebrate the appoint- ment of Bro Herbert Whitelegg, secretary of the Lymm Lodge, as Grand Master of the Warrington District. It is over 30 years since a Lymm Oddfellow held the office of Grand laster of the Warrington Oddfellows and then it was held by Mr James Whitelegg, father of the present holder of the office. Among the company present were representatives from six of the lodges in the Warrington district among whom were D.G.M. George Higham, P.G.M. Lester, P.P.G.M.'s J Norbury, R H Holford, Bradshaw, G F Freeman, and Lot Brooks' Robert Chorlton, N.C., Robert Hayes, V.G. ; P.G.'s John Whitlow, It Brooks, J Forrester, C E Ardern and W Challenor.</p>
